# Dashboard skip analytics and KPI detail panels
Workstream-ID: lea-09
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/1
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: dashboard.todo, completed feature bundle
Status: DONE
Milestone: Explain skipped jobs and drill into dashboard metrics
Dependencies: None

## Purpose
Make skipped-job totals, reasons and metric-specific detail available without
mixing skip events into the application-submission records.

## Tasks
- [x] Add the historical all-time skipped KPI.
- [x] Persist individual skip events separately from applications.
- [x] Show reason, time and job-metadata breakdowns and per-job details.
- [x] Add KPI cards that open category-specific inline detail panels.
- [x] Keep aggregation testable without importing Streamlit.
- [x] Update affected user and learning documentation.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Skip persistence/aggregation and focus-view behavior have recorded tests.
- [x] Navigation can dismiss the inline panel without changing application state.
- [x] The historical completed bundle has no recorded pending in-scope criteria.

## Completion evidence
The completed legacy dashboard record attributes nine cases to `test_skips.py`
and eight to `test_focus.py`. It identifies `Database.record_skip`,
`Database.skip_events`, `Orchestrator._note_skip`, `build_focus_view` and
the dashboard's skipped section/focus panel.
No date is invented for that undated source. These are attributed historical
implementation results, not tests rerun by this migration or human approval.
No database rows, screenshots containing applicant data or exported records are mirrored.

